course: dictionary
lesson: 6049
title: A candle holder with branches
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A menorah is a candle holder with branches, used in the Jewish religion. Its branches hold candles. It is a noun, so you can say one menorah or two menorahs.
explain: Read the context: «Hanukkah is a Jewish festival of lights that lasts eight nights, with a candle lit on the menorah each night.» The clues are festival, lights, eight nights and candle. So a menorah is something that holds candles during a festival of light.
explain: The dictionary gives three meanings. The nine-branched one, lit at Hanukkah, is also called a hanukkiah. The seven-branched one is an old symbol of Judaism. When a word has more than one meaning, check which one fits the sentence.
fact: A menorah is a candle holder with branches.
fact: The nine-branched menorah is lit during Hanukkah. It is also called a hanukkiah.
fact: The seven-branched menorah is an old symbol of Judaism.
fact: During Hanukkah, one more candle is lit each night for eight nights, plus a helper candle.
fact: Menorah is a noun: one menorah, two menorahs.
exercise: «Hanukkah is a Jewish festival of lights that lasts eight nights.» What is a menorah? | A type of bread | A festival that lasts eight nights | A kind of Christmas tree | *A candle holder with branches
exercise: On night 3 of Hanukkah, how many candles are lit on the menorah, not counting the helper candle? | 4 | 2 | *3 | 9
exercise: Find and copy the word that names a Jewish candle holder. | nights | eight | *menorah | festival
test: How many candles are lit in total over the eight nights, not counting the helper candle? | 8 | 16 | 44 | *36
test: What else is the nine-branched menorah called? | *A hanukkiah | A helper candle | A festival of lights | A seven-branched menorah
exam: Which meaning fits «the menorah stood on the table, shining with light»? | A kind of bread | A helper candle | A festival that lasts eight nights | *A candle holder with branches
